      "generated_answer": "The initial crowd has total \\(T\\) and adults \\(A\\) with \\(A = \\frac{5}{12}T \\Rightarrow T = \\frac{12}{5}A\\). Let \\(x\\) be the number of adults among the 50 new arrivals (\\(0 \\le x \\le 50\\)). After the bus, adults are \\(A + x\\) and total is \\(T + 50\\), giving \\(\\frac{A+x}{T+50} = \\frac{11}{25}\\). Substitute \\(T = \\frac{12}{5}A\\) to get \\(A + x = \\frac{132}{125}A + 22\\), so \\(x = 22 + \\frac{7A}{125}\\). For integer \\(x\\), \\(A\\) must be a multiple of 125; let \\(A = 125k\\). Then \\(x = 22 + 7k \\le 50\\) gives \\(k \\in \\{1,2,3,4\\}\\). Final adults \\(A + x = 125k + 22 + 7k = 132k + 22\\), which is minimized at \\(k=1\\) giving 154.\n\n\\boxed{154}",
