      "generated_answer": "The given polynomial simplifies to the generating function for partitions into parts 30, 42, 70, and 105, because for \\(0<x<1\\) we have \\(P(x) = (1-x^{2310})^6 \\prod_{d\\in\\{30,42,70,105\\}} (1-x^d)^{-1}\\). For the coefficient of \\(x^{2022}\\), the factor \\((1-x^{2310})^6\\) contributes only its constant term since \\(2310 > 2022\\), so the coefficient equals the number of nonnegative integer solutions to \\(30a+42b+70c+105d = 2022\\). Solving this Diophantine equation by parity and modular constraints reduces to \\(a_1+b_1+c_1+d' = 9\\) with nonnegative integers, yielding \\(\\binom{9+4-1}{3} = 220\\).\n\n\\boxed{220}",
