n 37. h4g5: hxg5. So h-pawn captured on g5. So no h-pawn.\n- a-pawn: 69. a2a4, captured by 70... Rxa2. So no a-pawn.\n- e-pawn: 27. e4f5 captured. No e-pawn.\n- f-pawn: 29. g4f5 captured? Wait, g4 captured f5. So f-pawn is gone? g-pawn: 25. g2g4, 29. g4f5 captured. So no g-pawn.\nSo White's pawns: d5, b5. Possibly c-pawn? c4 was there, pushed to c5 and captured by bxc5 and then Kxc5. So no c-pawn.\n\nWhite pieces: King on c5, Rook on d6, pawns on b5 and d5. Any other pieces? Bishops gone, knights gone, queen gone, other rook gone. So White has K, R, and two pawns.\n\nBlack:\nKing: Where is Black's king? Last move: 102... Kf5. Then 103. Re1, 104... Bg4, 105. Kd2, 106... Bf3, 107. Re8, 108... Bg2, 109. Kc3, 110... Be4, 111. Re6, 112... Bf3, 113. Bxb6, 114. cxb6, 115. Rxd6, 116... Rb7, 117. Kd4, 118... Bd1+, 119. c5, 120... bxc5, 121. Kxc5. The Black king hasn't moved since 102... Kf5? Wait, move 96... Kf5? 96. g6f5? Let's check: 80... Kg6, 81. Rh1, 82... Be2, 83. Kc3, 84... Re4, 85. Bd4, 86... Rf4, 87. Re1, 88... Re4, 89. Rg1, 90... Rg4, 91. Rh1, 92... Rf4, 93. Rh8, 94... Rf7, 95. Rg8, 96... Kf5 (King from g6 to f5). 97. Rc8, 98... Kg6? Wait, 98. f5g6? That's Black move 98? Let's recount:\n95. h8g8 (White) - Rh8 to g8? Wait, 93. h1h8 (Rh8), 94... f4f7 (Rf7), 95. h8g8 (Rg8). 96. g6f5 (Black Kf5). 97. g8c8 (White Rc8). 98. f5g6 (Black Kg6? But the move says \"f5g6\". That's King from f5 to g6? Yes, Kg6). 99. c8e8 (White Re8). 100. e2d1 (Black Bd1). 101. e8e6 (Re6). 102. g6f5 (Kf5). 103. e6e1 (Re1). 104. d1g4 (Bg4). 105. c3d2 (Kd2). 106. g4f3 (Bf3). 107. e1e8 (Re8). 108",
