      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve() -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Reads multiple test cases from stdin, each with an array of digits.\n    For each test case, computes the maximum product possible by adding\n    exactly 1 to one digit, and prints the result.\n    \"\"\"\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    \n    it = iter(data)\n    t = int(next(it))\n    out = []\n    \n    for _ in range(t):\n        n = int(next(it))\n        a = [int(next(it)) for _ in range(n)]\n        max_prod = 0\n        \n        # Try adding 1 to each element exactly once and compute the product.\n        for i in range(n):\n            a[i] += 1\n            prod = 1\n            for x in a:\n                prod *= x\n            if prod > max_prod:\n                max_prod = prod\n            a[i] -= 1  # revert\n            \n        out.append(str(max_prod))\n        \n    sys.stdout.write(\"\\n\".join(out))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
