      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef matrixScore(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the final score by repeatedly selecting the largest number\n    from each row, then adding the maximum of those selected numbers to the score.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Sort each row in descending order so we can process columns easily\n    sorted_rows = [sorted(row, reverse=True) for row in nums]\n    \n    # Find the maximum row length to know how many iterations we need\n    max_len = max(len(row) for row in sorted_rows) if sorted_rows else 0\n    \n    score = 0\n    # Process column by column\n    for col in range(max_len):\n        max_val = -1  # Since all numbers are >= 0, -1 works as a lower bound\n        for row in sorted_rows:\n            if col < len(row):\n                max_val = max(max_val, row[col])\n        score += max_val\n        \n    return score\n```",
