      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef shortest_subarray_sum(nums, target):\n    n = len(nums)\n    total = sum(nums)\n    q, r = divmod(target, total)\n    \n    # If target is exactly a multiple of total, we can just take q full copies\n    if r == 0:\n        return q * n\n    \n    # Otherwise, we need q full copies and a remainder r < total.\n    # The shortest remainder subarray will be found in two concatenated copies.\n    arr = nums + nums\n    left = 0\n    curr_sum = 0\n    min_len = float('inf')\n    \n    for right in range(len(arr)):\n        curr_sum += arr[right]\n        # Shrink window while sum exceeds r\n        while curr_sum > r and left <= right:\n            curr_sum -= arr[left]\n            left += 1\n        # If exact sum found, update minimum length\n        if curr_sum == r:\n            min_len = min(min_len, right - left + 1)\n    \n    if min_len == float('inf'):\n        return -1\n        \n    return q * n + min_len\n```",
