    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumSteps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the minimum number of adjacent swaps needed to group all '1's\n    to the right and all '0's to the left in the binary string s.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    # Collect the starting indices of all black balls ('1')\n    ones = [i for i, ch in enumerate(s) if ch == '1']\n    k = len(ones)\n    # The target positions of the ones when all are grouped to the right\n    target_start = n - k\n    # Each one at index ones[i] needs to move to target_start + i\n    # Since target_start + i >= ones[i], we sum the non-negative differences\n    return sum((target_start + i) - pos for i, pos in enumerate(ones))\n```",
