    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef numberOfGoodPartitions(nums):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    n = len(nums)\n    \n    # Step 1: record the last occurrence index for each number\n    last = {}\n    for i, x in enumerate(nums):\n        last[x] = i\n    \n    # Step 2: count how many \"blocks\" exist\n    blocks = 0\n    max_last = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        max_last = max(max_last, last[nums[i]])\n        if max_last == i:\n            blocks += 1\n            \n    # Step 3: the number of good partitions is 2^(blocks - 1) % MOD\n    return pow(2, blocks - 1, MOD)\n```",
