      "generated_answer": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef minCost(source: str, target: str, original: List[str], changed: List[str], cost: List[int]) -> int:\n    INF = 10**18\n    # dist[i][j] will store the minimum cost to change character i to character j\n    dist = [[INF] * 26 for _ in range(26)]\n    \n    # Cost to change a character to itself is 0\n    for i in range(26):\n        dist[i][i] = 0\n    \n    # Initialize the graph with the given direct transformations\n    for o, c, w in zip(original, changed, cost):\n        u = ord(o) - 97\n        v = ord(c) - 97\n        if w < dist[u][v]:\n            dist[u][v] = w\n    \n    # Floyd-Warshall algorithm to find all-pairs shortest paths\n    for k in range(26):\n        for i in range(26):\n            if dist[i][k] == INF:\n                continue\n            for j in range(26):\n                if dist[k][j] == INF:\n                    continue\n                new_dist = dist[i][k] + dist[k][j]\n                if new_dist < dist[i][j]:\n                    dist[i][j] = new_dist\n    \n    # Calculate the total minimum cost to convert source to target\n    total_cost = 0\n    for s_char, t_char in zip(source, target):\n        if s_char == t_char:\n            continue\n        u = ord(s_char) - 97\n        v = ord(t_char) - 97\n        if dist[u][v] == INF:\n            return -1\n        total_cost += dist[u][v]\n    \n    return total_cost\n```",
