      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef numberOfPowerfulInt(start: int, finish: int, limit: int, s: str) -> int:\n    def count(x: int) -> int:\n        s_int = int(s)\n        if x < s_int:\n            return 0\n        x_str = str(x)\n        n = len(x_str)\n        lenS = len(s)\n        res = 0\n        \n        # numbers with length strictly less than n\n        for L in range(lenS, n):\n            prefix_len = L - lenS\n            if prefix_len == 0:\n                res += 1\n            else:\n                # first digit of prefix: 1..limit, remaining digits: 0..limit\n                res += limit * ((limit + 1) ** (prefix_len - 1))\n        \n        # numbers with length exactly n\n        prefix_len = n - lenS\n        if prefix_len == 0:\n            res += 1\n        else:\n            x_prefix = x_str[:prefix_len]\n            x_suffix = x_str[prefix_len:]\n            valid = True\n            for i, ch in enumerate(x_prefix):\n                d = int(ch)\n                low = 1 if i == 0 else 0\n                high = min(d - 1, limit)\n                if low <= high:\n                    rem = prefix_len - i - 1\n                    res += (high - low + 1) * ((limit + 1) ** rem)\n                if d < low or d > limit:\n                    valid = False\n                    break\n            if valid and s <= x_suffix:\n                res += 1\n        return res\n    \n    return count(finish) - count(start - 1)\n```",
