    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Here’s an executable Python function that solves the problem using the described approach:\n\n```python\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef maxPalindromesAfterSwaps(words):\n    total_letters = Counter()\n    length_counts = Counter()\n    \n    for word in words:\n        total_letters.update(word)\n        length_counts[len(word)] += 1\n    \n    total_pairs = sum(count // 2 for count in total_letters.values())\n    single_letters = sum(count % 2 for count in total_letters.values())\n    \n    length_counts = sorted(length_counts.items())\n    max_palindromes = 0\n    \n    for length, count in length_counts:\n        needed_pairs_per_word = length // 2\n        for _ in range(count):\n            if total_pairs >= needed_pairs_per_word:\n                total_pairs -= needed_pairs_per_word\n                if length % 2 == 1:\n                    if single_letters > 0:\n                        single_letters -= 1\n                    elif total_pairs > 0:\n                        total_pairs -= 1\n                        single_letters += 1\n                    else:\n                        continue\n                max_palindromes += 1\n            else:\n                return max_palindromes\n\n    return max_palindromes\n```",
