    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef semiOrderedPermutation(nums: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the minimum number of adjacent swaps to make the permutation\n    semi-ordered (first element == 1 and last element == n).\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(nums)\n    idx1 = nums.index(1)\n    idxN = nums.index(n)\n    \n    # Moves needed: bring 1 to index 0 and n to index n-1\n    if idx1 < idxN:\n        return idx1 + (n - 1 - idxN)\n    else:\n        # When idx1 > idxN, one swap moves both 1 left and n right.\n        return idx1 + (n - 1 - idxN) - 1\n```",
