      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef longestSemiRepetitiveSubstring(s: str) -> int:\n    n = len(s)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return n\n    \n    max_len = 0\n    left = 0\n    pair_count = 0  # number of adjacent equal pairs in the window s[left:right+1]\n    \n    for right in range(n):\n        # If we are adding a character that creates a new equal pair with the previous character\n        if right > 0 and s[right] == s[right - 1]:\n            pair_count += 1\n        \n        # If we have more than one equal adjacent pair, shrink from left\n        while pair_count > 1 and left < right:\n            # If the character we are removing was part of a pair, decrease the count\n            if left + 1 <= right and s[left] == s[left + 1]:\n                pair_count -= 1\n            left += 1\n        \n        # Update max length\n        max_len = max(max_len, right - left + 1)\n    \n    return max_len\n```",
