input values are integers.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n7 6\n5\n6 1\n3 1\n4 2\n1 5\n6 2\n2\n2 5\n2\n3 4\n\nSample Output 1\n\n0 2\n\nThere are nine pieces in total: six with zero strawberries, one with one strawberry, and two with two strawberries. Therefore, when choosing just one of these pieces to eat, the minimum possible number of strawberries on the chosen piece is 0, and the maximum possible number is 2.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n4 4\n4\n1 1\n3 1\n3 3\n1 3\n1\n2\n1\n2\n\nSample Output 2\n\n1 1\n\nEach piece has one strawberry on it.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom bisect import bisect_left\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()\n    it = iter(data)\n    W = int(next(it))\n    H = int(next(it))\n    N = int(next(it))\n\n    p = [0] * N\n    q = [0] * N\n    for i in range(N):\n        p[i] = int(next(it))\n        q[i] = int(next(it))\n\n    A = int(next(it))\n    a = [0] * A\n    for i in range(A):\n        a[i] = int(next(it))\n\n    B = int(next(it))\n    b = [0] * B\n    for i in range(B):\n        b[i] = int(next(it))\n\n    counts = defaultdict(int)\n    for x, y in zip(p, q):\n        i = bisect_left(a, x)\n        j = bisect_left(b, y)\n        counts[(i, j)] += 1\n\n    total_cells = (A + 1) * (B + 1)\n    non_empty = len(counts)\n\n    if non_empty < total_cells:\n        min_straw = 0\n    else:\n        min_straw = min(counts.values())\n\n    max_straw = max(counts.values())\n    print(f\"{min_straw} {max_straw}\")\n```",
