      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    from collections import deque\n\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    H = int(data[0])\n    W = int(data[1])\n    grid = data[2:]\n\n    target = \"snuke\"\n    # mapping not strictly necessary, can just use target string\n    if grid[0][0] != 's':\n        print(\"No\")\n        return\n\n    # visited[r][c][mod] where mod is the index in \"snuke\" corresponding to the cell\n    visited = [[[False] * 5 for _ in range(W)] for _ in range(H)]\n    q = deque()\n    q.append((0, 0, 0))  # (row, col, mod)\n    visited[0][0][0] = True\n\n    dirs = [(1, 0), (-1, 0), (0, 1), (0, -1)]\n\n    while q:\n        r, c, mod = q.popleft()\n        if r == H - 1 and c == W - 1:\n            print(\"Yes\")\n            return\n        nmod = (mod + 1) % 5\n        for dr, dc in dirs:\n            nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n            if 0 <= nr < H and 0 <= nc < W and not visited[nr][nc][nmod]:\n                if grid[nr][nc] == target[nmod]:\n                    visited[nr][nc][nmod] = True\n                    q.append((nr, nc, nmod))\n\n    print(\"No\")\n```",
