    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve() -> None:\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    N = int(data[0])\n    grid = [list(row) for row in data[1:1+N]]\n    \n    # Collect border coordinates in clockwise order starting from (0,0)\n    border_coords = []\n    # Top row: left to right\n    for j in range(N):\n        border_coords.append((0, j))\n    # Right column: top to bottom (excluding the first element which is the corner already added)\n    for i in range(1, N):\n        border_coords.append((i, N-1))\n    # Bottom row: right to left (excluding the last corner)\n    for j in range(N-2, -1, -1):\n        border_coords.append((N-1, j))\n    # Left column: bottom to top (excluding the corners already added)\n    for i in range(N-2, 0, -1):\n        border_coords.append((i, 0))\n    \n    # Extract current border values\n    border_vals = [grid[r][c] for r, c in border_coords]\n    \n    # Rotate clockwise by one position\n    rotated = [border_vals[-1]] + border_vals[:-1]\n    \n    # Place the rotated values back into the grid\n    for (r, c), val in zip(border_coords, rotated):\n        grid[r][c] = val\n        \n    # Output the resulting grid\n    for row in grid:\n        print(''.join(row))\n\n```",
