      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef punishment_number(n: int) -> int:\n    def can_partition(s: str, target: int, index: int, current_sum: int) -> bool:\n        # If we've reached the end of the string, check if the sum equals the target\n        if index == len(s):\n            return current_sum == target\n        \n        # Try all possible splits from the current index\n        for j in range(index, len(s)):\n            # Take substring s[index:j+1] as the next part\n            part = int(s[index:j+1])\n            # If adding this part already exceeds target, no need to check further\n            # since all subsequent parts will be larger (positive integers)\n            if current_sum + part > target:\n                break\n            # Recursively check the rest of the string\n            if can_partition(s, target, j + 1, current_sum + part):\n                return True\n        return False\n\n    total = 0\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        sq = i * i\n        if can_partition(str(sq), i, 0, 0):\n            total += sq\n    return total\n```",
