      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n\n    def input():\n        return sys.stdin.readline().rstrip()\n\n    N, T, M = map(int, input().split())\n    incompatible = [set() for _ in range(N)]\n    for _ in range(M):\n        a, b = map(int, input().split())\n        a -= 1\n        b -= 1\n        incompatible[a].add(b)\n        incompatible[b].add(a)\n\n    # Precompute valid subsets: no incompatible pair inside\n    valid = [True] * (1 << N)\n    for mask in range(1 << N):\n        if not valid[mask]:\n            continue\n        # Check if mask contains any incompatible pair\n        # Iterate over bits in mask\n        m = mask\n        while m:\n            lsb = m & -m\n            i = (lsb.bit_length() - 1)\n            # Check against other bits in mask\n            m2 = m ^ lsb\n            while m2:\n                lsb2 = m2 & -m2\n                j = (lsb2.bit_length() - 1)\n                if j in incompatible[i]:\n                    valid[mask] = False\n                    break\n                m2 ^= lsb2\n            if not valid[mask]:\n                break\n            m ^= lsb\n\n    # dp[mask][k] = number of valid unlabeled partitions of subset 'mask' into exactly k blocks\n    dp = [[0] * (T + 1) for _ in range(1 << N)]\n    dp[0][0] = 1\n\n    for mask in range(1, 1 << N):\n        # Find lowest set bit\n        lsb = mask & -mask\n        rest = mask ^ lsb\n        # Iterate submasks of 'rest', then add lsb\n        sub = rest\n        while True:\n            submask = sub | lsb\n            if valid[submask]:\n                rem_mask = mask ^ submask\n                for k in range(1, T + 1):\n                    dp[mask][k] += dp[rem_mask][k - 1]\n            if sub == 0:\n                break\n            sub = (sub - 1) & rest\n\n    print(dp[(1 << N) - 1][T])\n```",
