      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve() -> None:\n    MOD = 998244353\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    N = int(data[0])\n    A = list(map(int, data[1:1 + N]))\n\n    # dp[mask] = probability that achievable subset sums correspond to mask\n    # mask bits 0..10 (bit i means sum i is achievable)\n    dp = [0] * 2048\n    dp[1] = 1  # only sum 0 is achievable initially\n\n    for a in A:\n        new_dp = [0] * 2048\n        inv_a = pow(a, MOD - 2, MOD)\n        prob_v = inv_a  # probability of each face 1..10 (if present)\n        prob_gt = 0\n        if a > 10:\n            prob_gt = (a - 10) * inv_a % MOD\n\n        for mask in range(2048):\n            cur = dp[mask]\n            if cur == 0:\n                continue\n            # faces > 10 do not change achievable sums\n            if prob_gt:\n                new_dp[mask] = (new_dp[mask] + cur * prob_gt) % MOD\n            # faces 1 .. min(10, a)\n            for v in range(1, min(10, a) + 1):\n                new_mask = mask | ((mask << v) & 2047)\n                new_dp[new_mask] = (new_dp[new_mask] + cur * prob_v) % MOD\n        dp = new_dp\n\n    target = 1 << 10\n    ans = sum(dp[mask] for mask in range(2048) if mask & target) % MOD\n    print(ans)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
