      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve() -> None:\n    import sys\n\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    it = iter(data)\n    N = int(next(it))\n    M = int(next(it))\n\n    # strong[i][j] is True if we know person i is stronger than person j\n    strong = [[False] * N for _ in range(N)]\n\n    for _ in range(M):\n        a = int(next(it)) - 1\n        b = int(next(it)) - 1\n        strong[a][b] = True\n\n    # Floyd–Warshall to compute transitive closure\n    for k in range(N):\n        for i in range(N):\n            if strong[i][k]:\n                for j in range(N):\n                    if strong[k][j]:\n                        strong[i][j] = True\n\n    # Strongest candidates are those with no known incoming edges\n    candidates = []\n    for i in range(N):\n        has_incoming = False\n        for j in range(N):\n            if i != j and strong[j][i]:\n                has_incoming = True\n                break\n        if not has_incoming:\n            candidates.append(i + 1)\n\n    if len(candidates) == 1:\n        print(candidates[0])\n    else:\n        print(-1)\n```",
