      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    it = iter(data)\n    N = int(next(it))\n    winners = []\n    min_bets = float('inf')\n    for i in range(1, N + 1):\n        C = int(next(it))\n        bets = set()\n        for _ in range(C):\n            bets.add(int(next(it)))\n        X = None  # will be read after the loop, but we need X to compare\n        # Actually we need X for comparisons. X is at the end.\n        # So we must store the bets for each person and then process after reading X.\n    # The above loop cannot check X yet because X is the last token.\n    # Let's fix: read all data first.\n    \n# Rewriting properly:\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    it = iter(data)\n    N = int(next(it))\n    people = []\n    for i in range(1, N + 1):\n        C = int(next(it))\n        bets = set()\n        for _ in range(C):\n            bets.add(int(next(it)))\n        people.append((i, C, bets))\n    X = int(next(it))\n    \n    winners = []\n    min_bets = float('inf')\n    for i, C, bets in people:\n        if X in bets:\n            if C < min_bets:\n                min_bets = C\n                winners = [i]\n            elif C == min_bets:\n                winners.append(i)\n    \n    print(len(winners))\n    if winners:\n        print(' '.join(map(str, winners)))\n    else:\n        print()\n```",
