    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve() -> None:\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    it = iter(data)\n    N = int(next(it))\n    M = int(next(it))\n    L = [int(next(it)) for _ in range(N)]\n\n    # The minimum possible width is at least the maximum word length.\n    low = max(L)\n    # The maximum possible width is all words in a single line.\n    high = sum(L) + N - 1\n\n    def lines_needed(W: int) -> int:\n        lines = 1\n        current_width = 0\n        for length in L:\n            if current_width == 0:\n                current_width = length\n            else:\n                if current_width + 1 + length <= W:\n                    current_width += 1 + length\n                else:\n                    lines += 1\n                    current_width = length\n        return lines\n\n    # Binary search for the minimal width such that lines_needed <= M.\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if lines_needed(mid) <= M:\n            high = mid\n        else:\n            low = mid + 1\n\n    print(low)\n```",
