    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve() -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Reads N, X, and N-1 scores from standard input.\n    Prints the minimum score needed in round N to achieve a final grade >= X,\n    or -1 if impossible.\n    \"\"\"\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n\n    N = int(data[0])\n    X = int(data[1])\n    A = list(map(int, data[2:]))\n\n    # Precompute sum of known scores\n    sum_A = sum(A)\n\n    # Minimum possible score is 0, maximum is 100\n    for s in range(101):\n        # The final grade is the sum of all scores minus the smallest and largest\n        total = sum_A + s\n        min_val = min(s, min(A))  # A is non-empty because N >= 3 => N-1 >= 2\n        max_val = max(s, max(A))\n        if total - min_val - max_val >= X:\n            print(s)\n            return\n\n    # No score in [0, 100] works\n    print(-1)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
