      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    it = iter(data)\n    N = int(next(it))\n    D = [int(next(it)) for _ in range(N)]\n    L1 = int(next(it))\n    C1 = int(next(it))\n    K1 = int(next(it))\n    L2 = int(next(it))\n    C2 = int(next(it))\n    K2 = int(next(it))\n\n    INF = 10**15\n    # dp[j] = minimum total type-2 sensors used when using exactly j type-1 sensors\n    dp = [INF] * (K1 + 1)\n    dp[0] = 0\n\n    for d in D:\n        new_dp = [INF] * (K1 + 1)\n        for x in range(K1 + 1):\n            # Minimum type-2 sensors needed if we use x type-1 sensors for this section\n            rem = d - x * L1\n            if rem <= 0:\n                y = 0\n            else:\n                y = (rem + L2 - 1) // L2\n            if y > K2:\n                # Even if we use no type-2 elsewhere, we would exceed K2\n                continue\n            for used in range(K1 - x + 1):\n                if dp[used] != INF:\n                    new_y = dp[used] + y\n                    if new_y < new_dp[used + x]:\n                        new_dp[used + x] = new_y\n        dp = new_dp\n\n    ans = INF\n    for j in range(K1 + 1):\n        if dp[j] <= K2:\n            cost = C1 * j + C2 * dp[j]\n            if cost < ans:\n                ans = cost\n\n    if ans == INF:\n        print(-1)\n    else:\n        print(ans)\n```",
