    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom itertools import permutations\n\ndef solve() -> None:\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    it = iter(data)\n    H = int(next(it))\n    W = int(next(it))\n\n    A = [[int(next(it)) for _ in range(W)] for _ in range(H)]\n    B = [[int(next(it)) for _ in range(W)] for _ in range(H)]\n\n    # Precompute inversion counts for all permutations of 0..H-1 and 0..W-1\n    def inv_count(perm):\n        # permutation as tuple of ints\n        c = 0\n        n = len(perm)\n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(i+1, n):\n                if perm[i] > perm[j]:\n                    c += 1\n        return c\n\n    row_perms = list(permutations(range(H)))\n    col_perms = list(permutations(range(W)))\n\n    row_inv = {p: inv_count(p) for p in row_perms}\n    col_inv = {p: inv_count(p) for p in col_perms}\n\n    min_ops = float('inf')\n\n    for rp in row_perms:\n        for cp in col_perms:\n            # check if A[rp[i]][cp[j]] == B[i][j]\n            ok = True\n            for i in range(H):\n                # Quick early break if possible: we can check row by row\n                rowA = A[rp[i]]\n                rowB = B[i]\n                for j in range(W):\n                    if rowA[cp[j]] != rowB[j]:\n                        ok = False\n                        break\n                if not ok:\n                    break\n            if ok:\n                ops = row_inv[rp] + col_inv[cp]\n                if ops < min_ops:\n                    min_ops = ops\n\n    if min_ops == float('inf'):\n        print(-1)\n    else:\n        print(min_ops)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
