    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef count_servers(n: int, logs: List[List[int]], x: int, queries: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n    # Find the maximum time value to size the BIT properly\n    max_time = max(queries)\n    if logs:\n        max_time = max(max_time, max(t for _, t in logs))\n    \n    # Binary Indexed Tree (Fenwick Tree) for frequencies of last request times\n    bit = [0] * (max_time + 2)  # 1-indexed, size max_time+2 to be safe\n    \n    def update(i: int, delta: int) -> None:\n        while i < len(bit):\n            bit[i] += delta\n            i += i & -i\n            \n    def query(i: int) -> int:\n        s = 0\n        while i > 0:\n            s += bit[i]\n            i -= i & -i\n        return s\n    \n    # Sort logs by time\n    logs_sorted = sorted(logs, key=lambda entry: entry[1])\n    # Sort queries by query time, keeping original indices\n    queries_sorted = sorted(enumerate(queries), key=lambda q: q[1])\n    \n    # last_time[server_id] = most recent request time seen so far\n    last_time = [0] * (n + 1)\n    ans = [0] * len(queries)\n    \n    log_idx = 0\n    m = len(logs_sorted)\n    \n    for idx, q in queries_sorted:\n        # Process all logs with time <= q\n        while log_idx < m and logs_sorted[log_idx][1] <= q:\n            server, t = logs_sorted[log_idx]\n            old = last_time[server]\n            if t > old:\n                if old > 0:\n                    update(old, -1)\n                update(t, 1)\n                last_time[server] = t\n            log_idx += 1\n        \n        L = q - x\n        if L < 1:\n            L = 1  # Times are >= 1, but x < queries[i] ensures L >= 1 normally.\n        # Number of servers with last request time >= L\n        cnt = query(max_time) - query(L - 1)\n        ans[idx] = n - cnt\n        \n    return ans\n```",
