      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    input = sys.stdin.readline\n    N = int(input())\n    adj = [[] for _ in range(N + 1)]\n    for _ in range(N - 1):\n        u, v = map(int, input().split())\n        adj[u].append(v)\n        adj[v].append(u)\n    C = [0] + list(map(int, input().split()))\n    \n    total_C = sum(C)\n    parent = [0] * (N + 1)\n    depth = [0] * (N + 1)\n    order = []\n    stack = [1]\n    parent[1] = -1\n    \n    # First DFS to set parent, depth, and traversal order\n    while stack:\n        u = stack.pop()\n        order.append(u)\n        for v in adj[u]:\n            if v != parent[u]:\n                parent[v] = u\n                depth[v] = depth[u] + 1\n                stack.append(v)\n    \n    # Compute subtree sums of C in reverse order\n    sub_weight = [0] * (N + 1)\n    for u in reversed(order):\n        w = C[u]\n        for v in adj[u]:\n            if v != parent[u]:\n                w += sub_weight[v]\n        sub_weight[u] = w\n    \n    # Initial f(1)\n    f1 = 0\n    for i in range(1, N + 1):\n        f1 += C[i] * depth[i]\n    \n    # Second pass to compute all f(v) and track minimum\n    min_f = f1\n    f = [0] * (N + 1)\n    f[1] = f1\n    for u in order:\n        for v in adj[u]:\n            if v != parent[u]:\n                f[v] = f[u] + total_C - 2 * sub_weight[v]\n                if f[v] < min_f:\n                    min_f = f[v]\n    \n    print(min_f)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
