      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    N = int(data[0])\n    A = int(data[1])\n    X = int(data[2])\n    Y = int(data[3])\n    \n    memo = {}\n    \n    def f(n):\n        if n == 0:\n            return 0.0\n        if n in memo:\n            return memo[n]\n        \n        # Option 1: pay X and replace N with N // A\n        res = X + f(n // A)\n        \n        # Option 2: pay Y and roll a die\n        # We already solved the self-loop for outcome 1:\n        # E = Y + (1/6)*E + (1/6)*sum_{b=2..6} f(n // b)\n        # => E = (6*Y + sum_{b=2..6} f(n // b)) / 5\n        s = f(n // 2) + f(n // 3) + f(n // 4) + f(n // 5) + f(n // 6)\n        roll = (6.0 * Y + s) / 5.0\n        \n        if roll < res:\n            res = roll\n            \n        memo[n] = res\n        return res\n    \n    ans = f(N)\n    # Print with sufficient precision\n    print(f\"{ans:.15f}\")\n```",
