    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef solve() -> None:\n    input = sys.stdin.readline\n    H, W = map(int, input().split())\n    grid = [input().strip() for _ in range(H)]\n\n    # directions\n    dirs = [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]\n\n    # 1. determine which empty cells are 'safe' (no adjacent magnet)\n    safe = [[False] * W for _ in range(H)]\n    has_safe = False\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if grid[i][j] == '.':\n                ok = True\n                for di, dj in dirs:\n                    ni, nj = i + di, j + dj\n                    if 0 <= ni < H and 0 <= nj < W and grid[ni][nj] == '#':\n                        ok = False\n                        break\n                if ok:\n                    safe[i][j] = True\n                    has_safe = True\n\n    if not has_safe:\n        # all empty cells are non-safe -> degree 1 for each\n        print(1)\n        return\n\n    visited_safe = [[False] * W for _ in range(H)]\n    comp_id = [[-1] * W for _ in range(H)]  # for non-safe empty cells\n    cid = 0\n    max_degree = 0\n\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if safe[i][j] and not visited_safe[i][j]:\n                cid += 1\n                q = deque()\n                q.append((i, j))\n                visited_safe[i][j] = True\n                safe_count = 0\n                non_safe_count = 0\n\n                while q:\n                    r, c = q.popleft()\n                    safe_count += 1\n                    for dr, dc in dirs:\n                        nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n                        if 0 <= nr < H and 0 <= nc < W:\n                            if safe[r][c]:  # current is safe\n                                # neighbor\n                                if safe[nr][nc] and not visited_safe[nr][nc]:\n                                    visited_safe[nr][nc] = True\n                                    q.append((nr, nc))\n                                elif grid[nr][nc] == '.' and not safe[nr][nc]:\n                                    if comp_id[nr][nc] != cid:\n                                        comp_id[nr][nc] = cid\n                                        non_safe_count += 1\n                degree = safe_count + non_safe_count\n                if degree > max_degree:\n                    max_degree = degree\n\n    # Also check isolated non-safe empty cells?\n    # They have degree 1, and max_degree is at least 1 from safe components.\n    # But if all empty cells are non-safe, we already handled that.\n    # If there are safe components, max_degree >= safe_component size >= 1,\n    # so isolated non-safe cells can't exceed the max.\n    print(max_degree)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
