    "global index": "LiveCodeBench_45",
    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. Return the function body without invoking it at the final solution. Question:\nYou are given a 0-indexed integer array nums containing n distinct positive integers. A permutation of nums is called special if:\n\nFor all indexes 0 <= i < n - 1, either nums[i] % nums[i+1] == 0 or nums[i+1] % nums[i] == 0.\n\nReturn the total number of special permutations. As the answer could be large, return it modulo 10^9 + 7.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: nums = [2,3,6]\nOutput: 2\nExplanation: [3,6,2] and [2,6,3] are the two special permutations of nums.\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: nums = [1,4,3]\nOutput: 2\nExplanation: [3,1,4] and [4,1,3] are the two special permutations of nums.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n2 <= nums.length <= 14\n1 <= nums[i] <= 10^9",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef specialPerm(nums):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    n = len(nums)\n    \n    # Precompute which pairs (i, j) satisfy the divisibility condition\n    divisible = [[False] * n for _ in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(n):\n            if i != j:\n                if nums[i] % nums[j] == 0 or nums[j] % nums[i] == 0:\n                    divisible[i][j] = True\n                    \n    # dp[mask][last]: number of ways to form a permutation using the elements\n    # indicated by 'mask', ending with the element at index 'last'\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(1 << n)]\n    \n    # Base cases: permutations of length 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[1 << i][i] = 1\n        \n    # Iterate over all masks (visited subsets)\n    for mask in range(1 << n):\n        for last in range(n):\n            if not (mask & (1 << last)):\n                continue\n            ways = dp[mask][last]\n            if ways == 0:\n                continue\n            # Try to extend the permutation with a new element 'nxt'\n            for nxt in range(n):\n                if mask & (1 << nxt):\n                    continue\n                if divisible[last][nxt]:\n                    new_mask = mask | (1 << nxt)\n                    dp[new_mask][nxt] = (dp[new_mask][nxt] + ways) % MOD\n                    \n    # Sum all permutations that use all elements\n    full_mask = (1 << n) - 1\n    ans = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        ans = (ans + dp[full_mask][i]) % MOD\n    return ans\n```",
