      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.readline\n    N, L, R = map(int, input().split())\n    size = 1 << N\n    \n    intervals = []\n    def add_intervals(l, r, nl, nr):\n        \"\"\"Standard segment tree decomposition of [l, r] into canonical intervals.\"\"\"\n        if l <= nl and nr <= r:\n            intervals.append((nl, nr))\n            return\n        mid = (nl + nr) // 2\n        if l <= mid:\n            add_intervals(l, r, nl, mid)\n        if r > mid:\n            add_intervals(l, r, mid + 1, nr)\n    \n    add_intervals(L, R, 0, size - 1)\n    \n    ans = 0\n    for nl, nr in intervals:\n        length = nr - nl + 1        # length = 2^i\n        i = length.bit_length() - 1\n        j = nl // length\n        print(f\"? {i} {j}\", flush=True)\n        T = int(input().strip())\n        if T == -1:\n            sys.exit(0)\n        ans = (ans + T) % 100\n    \n    print(f\"! {ans}\", flush=True)\n```",
