    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Here’s one way to implement the solution efficiently using sorting and a Fenwick tree (Binary Indexed Tree):  \n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    intervals = []\n    idx = 1\n    for _ in range(n):\n        l = int(data[idx])\n        r = int(data[idx + 1])\n        idx += 2\n        intervals.append((l, r))\n    \n    # Count total pairs\n    total_pairs = n * (n - 1) // 2\n    \n    # Count non-intersecting pairs where interval i is completely to the left of interval j\n    # i.e., r_i < l_j\n    intervals.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n    \n    # Coordinate compression for r values\n    r_values = sorted(set(r for _, r in intervals))\n    compress = {v: i + 1 for i, v in enumerate(r_values)}\n    \n    class BIT:\n        def __init__(self, size):\n            self.size = size\n            self.tree = [0] * (size + 1)\n        def update(self, i, delta):\n            while i <= self.size:\n                self.tree[i] += delta\n                i += i & -i\n        def query(self, i):\n            s = 0\n            while i > 0:\n                s += self.tree[i]\n                i -= i & -i\n            return s\n    \n    bit = BIT(len(r_values))\n    non_intersecting = 0\n    \n    # Count pairs where r_i < l_j\n    for l, r in intervals:\n        # Number of intervals with r < current l\n        less_idx = compress[r] if r in compress else 0\n        # find count of r values < l\n        pos = 0\n        # binary search in compressed values for first r >= l\n        lo, hi = 0, len(r_values) - 1\n        while lo <= hi:\n            mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n            if r_values[mid] < l:\n                pos = mid + 1\n                lo = mid + 1\n            else:\n                hi = mid - 1\n        non_intersecting += bit.query(pos)\n        bit.update(compress[r], 1)\n    \n    print(total_pairs - non_intersecting)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
