      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minMoves(nums, k, maxChanges):\n    n = len(nums)\n    # positions of all existing ones in the array\n    P = [i for i, v in enumerate(nums) if v == 1]\n    M = len(P)\n\n    # If there are no existing ones, we must use maxChanges created ones.\n    if M == 0:\n        return 2 * k\n\n    # Allowed number of existing ones to collect\n    L = max(0, k - maxChanges)   # minimum we must collect\n    R = min(k, M)                # maximum we can collect\n\n    # prefix sums for fast distance computation\n    prefP = [0] * (M + 1)\n    for i in range(M):\n        prefP[i + 1] = prefP[i] + P[i]\n\n    def compute_cost(m):\n        \"\"\"Return an array of length n, where arr[i] = minimal moves to\n           collect m existing ones when starting at index i.\"\"\"\n        if m == 0:\n            return [0] * n\n        costs = [0] * n\n        l = 0          # left border of the optimal contiguous m-sized window in P\n        ptr = 0        # number of elements in P <= current i\n        for i in range(n):\n            # advance ptr so that P[ptr] is the first element > i\n            while ptr < M and P[ptr] <= i:\n                ptr += 1\n            # shift window right while the rightmost element is closer than the leftmost\n            while l + m < M:\n                if abs(P[l + m] - i) < abs(P[l] - i):\n                    l += 1\n                else:\n                    break\n            # number of window elements <= i\n            left_cnt = min(l + m, ptr) - l\n            if left_cnt < 0:\n                left_cnt = 0\n            right_cnt = m - left_cnt\n            sum_left = prefP[l + left_cnt] - prefP[l]\n            sum_right = prefP[l + m] - prefP[l + left_cnt]\n            # sum of distances for this window\n            cost = i * left_cnt - sum_left + sum_right - i * right_cnt\n            costs[i] = cost\n        return costs\n\n    cost_L = compute_cost(L) if L > 0 else [0] * n\n    cost_R = compute_cost(R) if R > 0 else [0] * n\n\n    ans = float('inf')\n    for i in range(n):\n        # c2 = number of existing ones within distance 2 from i\n        start = max(0, i - 2)\n        end = min(n, i + 3)\n        c2 = 0\n        for j in range(start, end):\n            if nums[j] == 1:\n                c2 += 1\n\n        # The optimal number of existing ones to collect is clamped C2\n        m_opt = max(L, min(R, c2))\n\n        if m_opt == L:\n            val = cost_L[i] + 2 * (k - L)\n        elif m_opt == R:\n            val = cost_R[i] + 2 * (k - R)\n        else:\n            # m_opt == c2 and it lies strictly between L and R\n            sum_dist = 0\n            for j in range(start, end):\n                if nums[j] == 1:\n                    sum_dist += abs(j - i)\n            val = sum_dist + 2 * (k - c2)\n        \n        if val < ans:\n            ans = val\n\n    return ans\n```",
