    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef mostFrequentIDs(nums, freq):\n    from collections import defaultdict\n    import heapq\n\n    count = defaultdict(int)          # stores current frequency of each ID\n    max_heap = []                     # max-heap simulated with negative counts\n    ans = []\n\n    for n, f in zip(nums, freq):\n        # Update frequency\n        count[n] += f\n        new_count = count[n]\n        # Push the new frequency into the heap\n        heapq.heappush(max_heap, (-new_count, n))\n        # Remove stale entries from the top of the heap\n        while max_heap:\n            c, id_ = max_heap[0]\n            c = -c\n            if count[id_] == c:\n                break\n            heapq.heappop(max_heap)\n        # The top of the heap is the current maximum frequency (0 if empty)\n        if max_heap:\n            ans.append(-max_heap[0][0])\n        else:\n            ans.append(0)\n\n    return ans\n```",
