      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef find_longest_common_suffix_indices(wordsContainer, wordsQuery):\n    # Precompute lengths of container words for fast comparisons\n    lengths = [len(w) for w in wordsContainer]\n    \n    # Trie representation using lists for memory and speed\n    # children[node] is a dict mapping character -> next node index\n    # best_idx[node] stores the index in wordsContainer of the best word among those\n    # that pass through this node.\n    children = [{}]\n    best_idx = [-1]\n    \n    def update(node: int, idx: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Update the best index at the given node according to the problem's tie-breaking rules.\"\"\"\n        curr = best_idx[node]\n        if curr == -1:\n            best_idx[node] = idx\n        else:\n            # Prefer shorter length; if equal, prefer smaller index\n            if lengths[idx] < lengths[curr] or (lengths[idx] == lengths[curr] and idx < curr):\n                best_idx[node] = idx\n    \n    # Insert all reversed words into the trie\n    for idx, w in enumerate(wordsContainer):\n        rev = w[::-1]\n        node = 0\n        update(node, idx)  # update root\n        for ch in rev:\n            nxt = children[node].get(ch)\n            if nxt is None:\n                nxt = len(children)\n                children.append({})\n                best_idx.append(-1)\n                children[node][ch] = nxt\n            node = nxt\n            update(node, idx)\n    \n    # Process each query\n    ans = []\n    for q in wordsQuery:\n        rev = q[::-1]\n        node = 0\n        for ch in rev:\n            if ch not in children[node]:\n                break\n            node = children[node][ch]\n        ans.append(best_idx[node])\n    \n    return ans\n```",
