    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef find_kth_smallest_amount(coins, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the k-th smallest amount that can be made using an infinite number\n    of coins of each given denomination, without combining different denominations.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Helper to compute least common multiple of two integers\n    def lcm(a, b):\n        return a // math.gcd(a, b) * b\n\n    n = len(coins)\n    subsets = []  # will store (lcm, sign) for each non-empty subset of coins\n\n    # Precompute all subsets using bitmasks\n    for mask in range(1, 1 << n):\n        l = 1\n        bits = 0\n        for i in range(n):\n            if mask & (1 << i):\n                bits += 1\n                l = lcm(l, coins[i])\n        sign = 1 if bits % 2 == 1 else -1\n        subsets.append((l, sign))\n\n    def count_upto(x):\n        \"\"\"Counts how many distinct amounts are <= x using inclusion-exclusion.\"\"\"\n        total = 0\n        for l, sgn in subsets:\n            if l > x:\n                continue\n            total += sgn * (x // l)\n        return total\n\n    # Binary search for the k-th smallest amount\n    low = 1\n    high = k * max(coins)  # upper bound: k times the largest coin\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if count_upto(mid) >= k:\n            high = mid\n        else:\n            low = mid + 1\n    return low\n```",
