      "generated_answer": "Here’s an executable Python function for that problem:  \n\n```python\ndef minimize_string_value(s: str) -> str:\n        s = list(s)\n        n = len(s)\n        count = [0] * 26\n        used_in_gap = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n        \n        # Forward pass to assign minimal characters for '?'\n        for i in range(n):\n            if s[i] == '?':\n                best_char = -1\n                for c in range(26):\n                    if best_char == -1 or count[c] < count[best_char]:\n                        best_char = c\n                s[i] = chr(ord('a') + best_char)\n                count[best_char] += 1\n            else:\n                count[ord(s[i]) - ord('a')] += 1\n        \n        # We must now ensure lexicographically smallest among minimal values\n        # Backward pass to adjust choices while keeping same count constraints\n        count = [0] * 26\n        for i in range(n):\n            if s[i] == '?':\n                best_char = 0\n                while count[best_char] > 0:\n                    best_char += 1\n                s[i] = chr(ord('a') + best_char)\n                count[best_char] += 1\n            else:\n                count[ord(s[i]) - ord('a')] += 1\n        \n        # Actually we need to recalculate properly:\n        count = [0] * 26\n        for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n            if s[i] == '?':\n                best_char = 25\n                for c in range(25, -1, -1):\n                    if count[c] < count[best_char]:\n                        best_char = c\n                s[i] = chr(ord('a') + best_char)\n            count[ord(s[i]) - ord('a')] += 1\n        \n        return ''.join(s)\n```",
