      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef sum_of_power(nums, k):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    n = len(nums)\n    # Only elements <= k can be part of a subset that sums to k\n    valid_nums = [x for x in nums if x <= k]\n    # dp[s][c] = number of subsets with sum s using exactly c elements\n    dp = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(k + 1)]\n    dp[0][0] = 1\n    for x in valid_nums:\n        for s in range(k, x - 1, -1):\n            for c in range(1, n + 1):\n                if dp[s - x][c - 1]:\n                    dp[s][c] = (dp[s][c] + dp[s - x][c - 1]) % MOD\n    # Precompute powers of two\n    pow2 = [1] * (n + 1)\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        pow2[i] = (pow2[i-1] * 2) % MOD\n    # Sum over all valid sizes\n    ans = 0\n    for c in range(n + 1):\n        if dp[k][c]:\n            ans = (ans + dp[k][c] * pow2[n - c]) % MOD\n    return ans\n```",
