      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef sum_of_powers(nums, k):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    nums.sort()\n    n = len(nums)\n    \n    # collect all positive differences between elements\n    diffs = set()\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            d = nums[j] - nums[i]\n            if d > 0:\n                diffs.add(d)\n    if not diffs:\n        return 0\n    \n    diffs = sorted(diffs)\n    \n    # count subsequences of length k with all adjacent differences >= D\n    def count_at_least(D):\n        # dp for length 1: one way ending at each index\n        dp = [1] * n\n        for length in range(2, k + 1):\n            new_dp = [0] * n\n            prefix = 0\n            j = 0\n            for i in range(n):\n                while j < i and nums[i] - nums[j] >= D:\n                    prefix = (prefix + dp[j]) % MOD\n                    j += 1\n                new_dp[i] = prefix\n            dp = new_dp\n        return sum(dp) % MOD\n    \n    ans = 0\n    prev_D = diffs[0]\n    f_curr = count_at_least(prev_D)\n    ans = (ans + prev_D * f_curr) % MOD\n    \n    for i in range(1, len(diffs)):\n        D = diffs[i]\n        f_curr = count_at_least(D)\n        ans = (ans + (D - prev_D) * f_curr) % MOD\n        prev_D = D\n        \n    return ans\n```",
