      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef countSubarrays(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the number of subarrays where the first and last elements\n    are equal to the largest element in the subarray.\n    \"\"\"\n    from collections import defaultdict\n    from bisect import bisect_right\n\n    n = len(nums)\n    \n    # next_greater[i] = first index j > i such that nums[j] > nums[i]\n    # if no such element, it remains n\n    next_greater = [n] * n\n    stack = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        while stack and nums[i] > nums[stack[-1]]:\n            idx = stack.pop()\n            next_greater[idx] = i\n        stack.append(i)\n    \n    # Group indices by value\n    pos = defaultdict(list)\n    for i, val in enumerate(nums):\n        pos[val].append(i)\n    \n    total = 0\n    # For each value, count valid (i, j) pairs\n    for indices in pos.values():\n        for idx_in_list, i in enumerate(indices):\n            R = next_greater[i] - 1  # Rightmost index that can be included\n            # Find how many indices of this value are in the range [i, R]\n            j = bisect_right(indices, R) - 1\n            count = j - idx_in_list + 1\n            total += count\n            \n    return total\n```",
