      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef medianOfUniquenessArray(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the median of the uniqueness array of nums.\n    The uniqueness array contains the number of distinct elements \n    in every subarray of nums, sorted in non-decreasing order.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(nums)\n    total_subarrays = n * (n + 1) // 2\n    median_index = (total_subarrays - 1) // 2\n    \n    # Helper to count subarrays with at most k distinct elements\n    def count_at_most(k):\n        freq = {}\n        left = 0\n        distinct = 0\n        count = 0\n        for right in range(n):\n            num = nums[right]\n            freq[num] = freq.get(num, 0) + 1\n            if freq[num] == 1:\n                distinct += 1\n            while distinct > k:\n                left_num = nums[left]\n                freq[left_num] -= 1\n                if freq[left_num] == 0:\n                    distinct -= 1\n                left += 1\n            count += right - left + 1\n        return count\n    \n    # The possible number of distinct elements is in [1, number of unique values in nums]\n    low = 1\n    high = len(set(nums))\n    \n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if count_at_most(mid) > median_index:\n            high = mid\n        else:\n            low = mid + 1\n            \n    return low\n```",
