    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\n\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef minimum_anagram_length(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the minimum possible length of string t such that s is a concatenation\n    of anagrams of t.\n    \"\"\"\n    n: int = len(s)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # total character counts\n    total: List[int] = [0] * 26\n    for ch in s:\n        total[ord(ch) - 97] += 1\n\n    # prefix sums for fast block frequency queries\n    pref: List[List[int]] = [[0] * 26]\n    for ch in s:\n        new_row: List[int] = pref[-1][:]\n        new_row[ord(ch) - 97] += 1\n        pref.append(new_row)\n\n    # collect all divisors of n\n    divisors: List[int] = []\n    i = 1\n    while i * i <= n:\n        if n % i == 0:\n            divisors.append(i)\n            if i != n // i:\n                divisors.append(n // i)\n        i += 1\n    divisors.sort(reverse=True)  # check larger k (smaller L) first\n\n    for k in divisors:           # k = number of anagram blocks\n        # every character's total count must be divisible by k\n        if any(total[c] % k != 0 for c in range(26)):\n            continue\n\n        expected: List[int] = [total[c] // k for c in range(26)]\n        L: int = n // k\n        valid: bool = True\n\n        for start in range(0, n, L):\n            end: int = start + L\n            for c in range(26):\n                if pref[end][c] - pref[start][c] != expected[c]:\n                    valid = False\n                    break\n            if not valid:\n                break\n\n        if valid:\n            return L\n\n    # Fallback (should never be reached because k=1 always works)\n    return n\n\n```",
