      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef min_balanced_partitions(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the minimum number of balanced substrings into which the string s\n    can be partitioned. A balanced string is one where every character that\n    appears in it occurs the exact same number of times.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    # dp[i] = min partitions for prefix s[:i]\n    dp = [float('inf')] * (n + 1)\n    dp[0] = 0\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        freq = [0] * 26\n        max_freq = 0\n        distinct = 0\n        # Expand substring s[j:i] by moving j backwards\n        for j in range(i - 1, -1, -1):\n            c = ord(s[j]) - ord('a')\n            if freq[c] == 0:\n                distinct += 1\n            freq[c] += 1\n            if freq[c] > max_freq:\n                max_freq = freq[c]\n            # Check if current substring s[j:i] is balanced\n            if distinct * max_freq == i - j:\n                dp[i] = min(dp[i], dp[j] + 1)\n\n    return dp[n]\n```",
