      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef min_changes(s: str, k: int) -> int:\n    n = len(s)\n    INF = 10**9\n    \n    # cost[i][j] = minimum changes to make substring s[i:j] semi-palindrome\n    cost = [[INF] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n)]\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 2, n + 1):  # semi-palindrome needs length >= 2\n            L = j - i\n            best = INF\n            # Try all valid divisors d\n            for d in range(1, L):\n                if L % d != 0:\n                    continue\n                m = L // d  # elements per remainder group\n                changes = 0\n                # For each remainder group, count mismatches against palindrome\n                for r in range(d):\n                    for t in range(m // 2):\n                        idx1 = i + r + t * d\n                        idx2 = i + r + (m - 1 - t) * d\n                        if s[idx1] != s[idx2]:\n                            changes += 1\n                if changes < best:\n                    best = changes\n            cost[i][j] = best\n    \n    # dp[t][i] = min changes for partitioning prefix length i into t substrings\n    dp = [[INF] * (n + 1) for _ in range(k + 1)]\n    dp[0][0] = 0\n    \n    for t in range(1, k + 1):\n        for i in range(t * 2, n + 1):  # at least 2 chars per substring\n            for j in range(t - 1, i):  # previous split point\n                if i - j >= 2 and dp[t-1][j] != INF and cost[j][i] != INF:\n                    val = dp[t-1][j] + cost[j][i]\n                    if val < dp[t][i]:\n                        dp[t][i] = val\n                        \n    return dp[k][n]\n```",
