      "generated_answer": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef max_sum_almost_unique_subarray(nums: List[int], m: int, k: int) -> int:\n    if len(nums) < k:\n        return 0\n    \n    freq = {}\n    window_sum = 0\n    \n    # Initialize the first window\n    for i in range(k):\n        num = nums[i]\n        freq[num] = freq.get(num, 0) + 1\n        window_sum += num\n    \n    max_sum = 0\n    if len(freq) >= m:\n        max_sum = window_sum\n    \n    # Slide the window\n    for i in range(k, len(nums)):\n        # Add the new right element\n        right_num = nums[i]\n        freq[right_num] = freq.get(right_num, 0) + 1\n        window_sum += right_num\n        \n        # Remove the left element that falls out of the window\n        left_num = nums[i - k]\n        freq[left_num] -= 1\n        if freq[left_num] == 0:\n            del freq[left_num]\n        window_sum -= left_num\n        \n        # Update max_sum if condition holds\n        if len(freq) >= m:\n            max_sum = max(max_sum, window_sum)\n    \n    return max_sum\n```",
