      "generated_answer": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef minOperations(nums: List[int], target: int) -> int:\n    # If the total sum of nums is less than target, it's impossible.\n    if sum(nums) < target:\n        return -1\n\n    # Count frequencies of each power of 2.\n    # nums[i] <= 2^30, target < 2^31, so 32 bits are enough.\n    cnt = [0] * 32\n    for num in nums:\n        power = num.bit_length() - 1\n        cnt[power] += 1\n\n    ops = 0\n\n    # Process bits from least significant to most significant.\n    for i in range(32):\n        if target & (1 << i):\n            if cnt[i] > 0:\n                # We already have this power.\n                cnt[i] -= 1\n            else:\n                # Find the smallest larger power available.\n                j = i + 1\n                while j < 32 and cnt[j] == 0:\n                    j += 1\n                if j == 32:\n                    # No larger power available to split.\n                    return -1\n\n                # Split the power at j down to i.\n                ops += j - i\n                cnt[j] -= 1\n                # Intermediate pieces (except the one consumed at i) are added.\n                for k in range(i, j):\n                    cnt[k] += 1\n\n        # Combine pairs of the current power into the next power\n        # because they can act as larger denominations for higher bits.\n        if i < 31:\n            cnt[i + 1] += cnt[i] // 2\n            cnt[i] %= 2\n\n    return ops\n```",
