      "generated_answer": "Here’s the executable Python function based on your description:  \n\n```python\ndef minCost(s1: str, s2: str, x: int) -> int:\n    diff = [i for i in range(len(s1)) if s1[i] != s2[i]]\n    m = len(diff)\n    if m % 2:\n        return -1\n    if m == 0:\n        return 0\n    if m == 2:\n        if diff[1] - diff[0] == 1:\n            return min(x, 1)\n        else:\n            return min(x, (diff[1] - diff[0]) * 1)\n    dp = [float('inf')] * (m + 1)\n    dp[0] = 0\n    for i in range(2, m + 1, 2):\n        dp[i] = min(dp[i], dp[i - 2] + min(x, diff[i - 1] - diff[i - 2]))\n        if i >= 4:\n            dp[i] = min(dp[i], dp[i - 4] + min(2 * x, (diff[i - 1] - diff[i - 2]) + (diff[i - 3] - diff[i - 4])))\n    return dp[m]\n```",
