    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let’s compare after-tax cash-on-cash returns:  \n\n- **Plan A**: $80,000 equity, NOI = $10,450 – $3,200 = $7,250; depreciation = $50,000 ÷ 40 = $1,250; taxable income = $6,000; tax = $2,400; after-tax cash flow = $7,250 – $2,400 = $4,850; return = 6.06%.  \n- **Plan B**: $30,000 loan at 4.5% → interest $1,350; taxable income = $7,250 – $1,250 – $1,350 = $4,650; tax = $1,860; cash flow = $7,250 – $1,350 – $1,860 = $4,040; equity = $50,000; return = 8.08%.  \n- **Plan C**: $60,000 loan at 5.25% → interest $3,150; taxable income = $7,250 – $1,250 – $3,150 = $2,850; tax = $1,140; cash flow = $7,250 – $3,150 – $1,140 = $2,960; equity = $20,000; return = 14.8%.  \n\nPlan C has the highest rate of return under the given numbers.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
