  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_530",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: You have just redesigned your kitchen. The new floor dimensions are 7'6\" × 11'8\". Now you want to cover the floor with linoleum, which sells for $1.79 per running foot in 6' width, what is the best way to cover the floor? How much will it cost?\n\nOptions: \nA. $48.60\nB. $26.85\nC. $30.99\nD. $42.56\nE. $29.99\nF. $38.40\nG. $31.50\nH. $23.94\nI. $20.12\nJ. $35.70\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let’s break it down:  \n\nThe floor is **7'6\" × 11'8\"**, which is **7.5 ft × 11.67 ft**. The linoleum is **6 ft wide**.  \n\nIf we run the 6 ft width across the 7.5 ft dimension, we need two strips: one 6 ft wide, and another 1.5 ft wide, each **11.67 ft long**.  \nTotal length = **11.67 + 11.67 = 23.34 running feet**.  \n\nAt **$1.79 per running foot**, cost = \\( 23.34 \\times 1.79 \\approx 41.78 \\), which is not an option — so that layout isn’t the cheapest.  \n\nThe smarter layout: run the 6 ft width along the 11.67 ft dimension.  \nWe need **11.67 ft / 6 ft ≈ 1.945** → 2 strips, each **7.5 ft long**.  \nTotal length = \\( 7.5 + 7.5 = 15 \\) running feet.  \nCost = \\( 15 \\times 1.79 = 26.85 \\).  \n\nThat matches option **B**.  \n\n\\boxed{B}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 200,
        "output_tokens": 266,
        "total_tokens": 466
