    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the 1974 dollar-value LIFO ending inventory, we convert each year's ending inventory to base-year prices using the given indices and track the layers. After the 1973 decrease reduced the 1972 layer, the 1974 base-year inventory increased by $3,700, creating a new layer at the 1974 index of 1.08. Adding this $3,996 layer to the remaining layers yields a total LIFO cost of approximately $25,086.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
