  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_620",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For a one-period binomial model for the price of a stock, you are given: (i) The period is one year. (ii) The stock pays no dividends. (iii) u =1.433, where u is one plus the rate of capital gain on the stock if the price goes up.  (iv) d = 0.756 , where d is one plus the rate of capital loss on the stock if the price goes down. (v) The continuously compounded annual expected return on the stock is 10%. What is the true probability of the stock price going up.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.58\nB. 0.75\nC. 0.55\nD. 0.30\nE. 0.40\nF. 0.60\nG. 0.65\nH. 0.70\nI. 0.52\nJ. 0.45\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The true probability \\( p \\) of the stock price going up is found by setting the expected stock price equal to \\( S_0 e^{0.10} \\) (since the continuously compounded expected return is 10%). This gives \\( p \\cdot u + (1-p) \\cdot d = e^{0.10} \\). Solving: \\( p = \\frac{e^{0.10} - d}{u - d} = \\frac{1.10517 - 0.756}{1.433 - 0.756} \\approx 0.5156 \\), which rounds to 0.52.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 253,
        "output_tokens": 2467,
        "total_tokens": 2720
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
    },
    "cost": 0.00902538,
    "for_optimality": false
  },
  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_625",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the cost of renting a compact car for 2 days and 4 hours, and driving it 364 miles? CAR RENTAL SCHEDULE Local and One-Way Car Rate per Day Rate per Week Rate for Extra Hours Compact $12.00 per day $.14 per mile gas included $60.00 per week $.14 per mile gas included $2.75 per hour over 24 $.14 per mile gas included Standard $16.00 per day $.16 per mile gas included $80.00 per day $.16 per mile gas included $2.75 per hour over 24 $.16 per mile gas included Luxury $20.00 per day $.18 per mile gas included $100.00 per day $.18 per mile gas included $2.75 per hour over 24 $.18 per mile gas included MINIMUM CHARGE: 24-hour rate INSURANCE: (per day or any part thereof): Collision, $1.20; Liability, $1.20\n\nOptions: \nA. $102.30\nB. $78.20\nC. $84.96\nD. $110.48\nE. $69.04\nF. $86.40\nG. $125.72\nH. $99.88\nI. $57.88\nJ. $93.16\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To calculate the cost: the time charge for 2 days + 4 extra hours is \\(2 \\times \\$12.00 + 4 \\times \\$2.75 = \\$35.00\\). The mileage charge is \\(364 \\times \\$0.14 = \\$50.96\\). Insurance (collision and liability) is charged per day or any part thereof; since 2 days and 4 hours spans parts of 3 days, the cost is \\(3 \\times (\\$1.20 + \\$1.20) = \\$7.20\\). The total is \\(\\$35.00 + \\$50.96 + \\$7.20 = \\$93.16\\).\n\n\\boxed{J}",
