    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The quadratic formula gives the solutions for \\(ax^2 + bx + c = 0\\) as \\(x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\\). For \\(x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0\\), \\(a=1\\), \\(b=-5\\), \\(c=6\\).  \nDiscriminant: \\((-5)^2 - 4(1)(6) = 25 - 24 = 1\\).  \nRoots: \\(x = \\frac{5 \\pm 1}{2}\\) → \\(x = \\frac{6}{2} = 3\\) and \\(x = \\frac{4}{2} = 2\\).  \nTherefore, the solutions are \\(x = 3\\) and \\(x = 2\\).\n\n\\boxed{D}",
