      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is H. An undirected graph has an Euler circuit if and only if every vertex has even degree and the graph is connected. A complete graph with 13 vertices (K₁₃) has all vertex degrees equal to 12 (even) and is connected, so it must have an Euler circuit. K₁₂ has odd degree 11, and any tree with 13 vertices has leaves with degree 1 (odd), so neither has an Euler circuit.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
