      "generated_answer": "The correct choice is J. Problem I is decidable by direct simulation for \\(n\\) steps. Problem III is decidable by simulating \\(M\\) and limiting the tape to \\(n-1\\) squares; since the number of configurations in bounded space is finite, halting or repetition must occur and reveals whether a new square is ever scanned. Problem II is undecidable because it requires determining whether \\(M\\) will ever print a 1 arbitrarily far into an unbounded future, which reduces to the undecidable blank-tape halting problem.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
