      "generated_answer": "We can compute P(A|B) using the law of total probability: P(A) = P(A|B)P(B) + P(A|¬B)P(¬B). Substituting the given values: 1/2 = P(A|B)*(1/3) + (1/4)*(2/3) → 1/2 = P(A|B)/3 + 1/6 → P(A|B)/3 = 1/3 → P(A|B) = 1.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
