      "generated_answer": "The EM algorithm for maximum likelihood estimation (MLE) alternates between an Expectation (E) step and a Maximization (M) step. To modify it for maximum a posteriori (MAP) estimation, a prior distribution over the parameters is incorporated. The E-step, which computes the expected complete-data log-likelihood \\( Q(\\theta, \\theta^{(t)}) = \\mathbb{E}[\\log P(X, Z \\mid \\theta) \\mid X, \\theta^{(t)}] \\), remains unchanged because the latent variable posterior depends only on the likelihood and observed data. The M-step is modified to maximize \\( Q(\\theta, \\theta^{(t)}) + \\log P(\\theta) \\) instead of just \\( Q(\\theta, \\theta^{(t)}) \\). Therefore, only the Maximization step requires modification.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
