      "generated_answer": "The condition that the ratio of any two root-to-leaf path lengths is at most \\(c\\) implies that the shortest path length \\(s\\) satisfies \\(s \\ge h/c\\). In a strictly binary tree, the minimum number of nodes for a shortest path length \\(s\\) is achieved by a perfect tree of height \\(s\\), giving \\(N \\ge 2^{s+1}-1 > 2^{h/c}\\). This simplifies to \\(h < c \\log_2(N)\\), which holds strictly for \\(N > 1\\). Among the options, this strict bound is the most precise characterization.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
