      "generated_answer": "The Durbin-Watson statistic is approximately equal to 2(1 − ρ), where ρ is the first-order autocorrelation coefficient. If the statistic is close to zero, then 2(1 − ρ) ≈ 0, which implies ρ ≈ +1. Therefore, the first-order autocorrelation coefficient is close to plus one.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
