    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The given MA process is \\(y_t = u_t - 3u_{t-1} + u_{t-2}\\). The characteristic roots come from solving \\(1 - 3z + z^2 = 0\\), but those roots are not among the options. However, if the coefficient of \\(u_{t-2}\\) was intended to be 2 (a common textbook example), the MA polynomial becomes \\(1 - 3z + 2z^2 = 0\\), which factors as \\((1 - z)(1 - 2z) = 0\\), yielding roots 1 and 0.5. Given the available choices, this makes A the most likely correct answer.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
