    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The preemphasis filter with power transfer function \\(|H_p(f)|^2 = k^2 f^2\\) increases the power of the modulating signal. To ensure the FM transmission bandwidth (Carson's rule) remains unchanged, the average power of the preemphasized signal must not exceed the power of the original signal. By equating the integrals of the original and filtered power spectral densities over the message bandwidth \\(f_m\\) and using the approximation \\(\\arctan(f_m/f_1) \\approx \\pi/2\\) (since \\(f_1 \\ll f_m\\)), the maximum allowable gain factor is \\(k^2 \\leq \\frac{\\pi}{f_1(2f_m - \\pi f_1)}\\).\n\n\\boxed{I}",
