      "generated_answer": "To find the entropy change for solidification at 1120 K, we calculate \\(\\Delta S\\) along a reversible path: heat liquid from 1120 K to 1356 K, solidify at 1356 K, and cool solid back to 1120 K. Using \\(\\Delta S_1 = \\int \\frac{C_p(l)}{T}dT\\), \\(\\Delta S_{\\text{solid}} = \\frac{\\Delta H^0}{1356}\\), and \\(\\Delta S_2 = \\int \\frac{C_p(s)}{T}dT\\), the total is \\(\\Delta S = 7.50 \\ln\\frac{1356}{1120} - \\frac{3100}{1356} + 5.41 \\ln\\frac{1120}{1356} + 1.5\\times10^{-3}(1120-1356) \\approx -2.23 \\text{ cal K}^{-1}\\text{ mol}^{-1}\\).\n\n\\boxed{C}",
