    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The steady-state response of a linear difference equation to a sinusoid is found using the frequency response. For the system \\(y[n] + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}y[n-1] = x[n]\\) with \\(x[n] = \\cos(\\frac{\\pi}{6}n)\\), the frequency response is \\(H(e^{j\\omega}) = \\frac{1}{1 + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}e^{-j\\omega}}\\). Evaluating at \\(\\omega = \\pi/6\\) gives magnitude \\(\\sqrt{3/7}\\) and phase \\(\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{3}}\\right)\\), leading to \\(y_{ss}[n] = \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{7}}\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}n + \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{3}}\\right)\\right)\\), which matches option I.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
