      "generated_answer": "The current through a capacitor is given by i(t) = dq/dt. Substituting v(t) into q(t) = 0.5v²(t) yields q(t) = 0.5(1 + 0.5 sin t)² = 0.5 + 0.5 sin t + 0.125 sin² t. Differentiating gives i(t) = 0.5 cos t + 0.25 sin t cos t = 0.5 cos t + 0.125 sin 2t.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
