    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10464",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the equation of a 25-cycle-current sine wave, having anrmsvalue of 30 amp, and what is the value of the current whenthe time is 0.005 sec ? What fraction of a cycle has the wavegone through in 0.005 sec ? Assume that the wave crossesthe time axis in a positive direction when the time is equalto zero.\n\nOptions: \nA. i= 42.4 sin 314t, 30 amp, 1/12 cycle\nB. i= 42.4 cos 157t, 25 amp, 1/6 cycle\nC. i= 30 sin 100t, 42.4 amp, 1/6 cycle\nD. i= 42.4 sin 157t, 30 amp, 1/8 cycle\nE. i= 42.4 cos 157t, 30 amp, 1/20 cycle\nF. i= 30 cos 157t, 42.4 amp, 1/4 cycle\nG. i= 30 sin 157t, 42.4 amp, 1/4 cycle\nH. i= 42.4 sin 50t, 35 amp, 1/10 cycle\nI. i= 60 sin 157t, 30 amp, 1/5 cycle\nJ. i= 30 sin 157t, 35 amp, 1/10 cycle\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is D.\n\nThe wave is a sine wave crossing zero positively at t=0, so its equation is \\(i = I_m \\sin(\\omega t)\\). With frequency 25 Hz, \\(\\omega = 2\\pi(25) = 50\\pi \\approx 157\\) rad/s. The peak current from 30 A RMS is \\(30\\sqrt{2} \\approx 42.4\\) A, giving \\(i = 42.4 \\sin(157t)\\). At \\(t = 0.005\\) s, the angle is \\(157 \\times 0.005 \\approx 0.785\\) rad (45°), so the current is \\(42.4 \\sin 45° \\approx 30\\) A. The period is \\(1/25 = 0.04\\) s, so in 0.005 s the wave completes \\(0.005 / 0.04 = 1/8\\) of a cycle.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
