    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10472",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let A= kr^nr̂(in spherical coordinates) Evaluate \\int\\int\\int_v \\nabla \\bulletAdv wherev is a sphere of radius a with center at the origin.\n\nOptions: \nA. 4\\pi k a^n+2\nB. \\pi k a^n+2\nC. 2\\pi k a^n+1\nD. 5\\pi k a^n+3\nE. 6\\pi k a^n+1\nF. 4\\pi k a^n+1\nG. 2\\pi k a^n+2\nH. 4\\pi k a^(n-1)\nI. 4\\pi k a^n\nJ. 3\\pi k a^n\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are given  \n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{A} = k r^n \\hat{\\mathbf{r}}\n\\]  \n\nin spherical coordinates. The divergence in spherical coordinates for a radial field is  \n\n\\[\n\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{A} = \\frac{1}{r^2} \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial r} \\left( r^2 A_r \\right)\n\\]  \n\nHere \\( A_r = k r^n \\), so  \n\n\\[\n\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{A} = \\frac{1}{r^2} \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial r} \\left( k r^{n+2} \\right) \n= k (n+2) r^{n-1}\n\\]  \n\nNow integrate over the sphere of radius \\(a\\):  \n\n\\[\n\\int_V \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{A} \\, dV \n= \\int_0^a k (n+2) r^{n-1} \\cdot 4\\pi r^2 \\, dr \n= 4\\pi k (n+2) \\int_0^a r^{n+1} dr\n\\]  \n\\[\n= 4\\pi k (n+2) \\frac{a^{n+2}}{n+2} \n= 4\\pi k a^{n+2}\n\\]  \n\nTherefore, correct answer is:  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{A}\n\\]",
      "success": true,
