    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is C because it satisfies all three parts:\n(a) A pure standing wave requires the reflected wave amplitude magnitude to equal the incident amplitude, so E₁ = -5 V/m (or +5 V/m).\n(b) The VSWR is (E + |E₁|)/(E - |E₁|) = (5 + 0.1)/(5 - 0.1) = 5.1/4.9 ≈ 1.04.\n(c) E_max = E + |E₁| = 5 + 0.6 = 5.6 V/m; E_min = E - |E₁| = 5 - 0.6 = 4.4 V/m.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
