    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10876",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: f(X) = [\\pi(1 + X^2)]^-1- \\infty < x < \\infty. If Y = X^2, what is the density function of Y ?\n\nOptions: \nA. h(y) = [2 / {{\\pi(1 + \\sqrt{{y}})}}] for y > 0 and = 0 otherwise\nB. h(y) = [2 / {{\\pi\\surdy(1 + y)}}]y > 0 and = 0otherwise\nC. h(y) = [1 / {{\\pi(1 + y^2)}}] for y > 0 and = 0 otherwise\nD. h(y) = [1 / {{2\\pi(1 + \\sqrt{{y}})}}] for y > 0 and = 0 otherwise\nE. h(y) = [1 / {{2\\pi(1 + y^2)}}] for y > 0 and = 0 otherwise\nF. h(y) = [e^(-y) / {{2\\pi\\sqrt{{1 + y}}] for y > 0 and = 0 otherwise\nG. h(y) = [1 / {{\\pi\\surdy(1 + y)}}]y > 0 and = 0otherwise\nH. h(y) = [1 / {{\\pi(2 + \\sqrt{{y}})}}] for y > 0 and = 0 otherwise\nI. h(y) = [1 / {{2\\pi\\surdy(1 + y)}}]y > 0 and = 0otherwise\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The density of \\( X \\) is  \n\\[\nf_X(x) = \\frac{1}{\\pi (1+x^2)}, \\quad -\\infty < x < \\infty.\n\\]  \nFor \\( Y = X^2 \\), we use the transformation method:  \n\\[\nh(y) = f_X(\\sqrt{y}) \\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}} + f_X(-\\sqrt{y}) \\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}} = \\frac{2}{\\pi(1+y)} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}} = \\frac{1}{\\pi \\sqrt{y}(1+y)}, \\quad y > 0.\n\\]  \nThis matches option **G**.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
