    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: All of the following are true regarding the function of neurons EXCEPT:\n\nOptions: \nA. The refractory period prevents the neuron from initiating a new action potential.\nB. The transmitting neuron secretes neurotransmitters into the synaptic cleft from its dendrites.\nC. An action potential is initiated when the axon hillock reaches the threshold potential.\nD. The action potential travels along the axon away from the cell body.\nE. Hyperpolarization occurs when the membrane potential becomes more negative than the resting potential.\nF. The flow of sodium into the neuron depolarizes the membrane in the first phase of an action potential.\nG. Hyperpolarization at the end of an action potential is one mechanism by which neurons limit the rate at which action potentials may fire.\nH. The neuron releases neurotransmitters into the synaptic cleft from the axon terminals.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
