      "generated_answer": "The Carlsbad Resolutions, like the Concert of Europe, were conservative measures spearheaded by Metternich to suppress liberal and nationalist movements threatening the traditional monarchical order established after Napoleon's defeat. The press law excerpt highlights censorship and control, key tools used to prevent the spread of revolutionary ideas across the German Confederation and Europe.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
