      "generated_answer": "The poem urges Americans to take up the \"burden\" of civilizing \"half-devil and half-child\" peoples by ending famine and disease, even if their efforts are met with ingratitude; this paternalistic call aligns with the belief that advanced nations have a duty to uplift less-developed ones.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
