      "generated_answer": "The discovery of a shell at the Trinil site with an intentionally engraved zigzag pattern is the primary evidence suggesting Homo erectus may have possessed an aesthetic sense and created art. Other options either misattribute later hominin behaviors to Homo erectus (like figurines, cave paintings, or musical instruments) or contain factual inaccuracies regarding brain size. This specific engraved shell, dated to roughly half a million years ago, represents the earliest known example of geometric engraving by a hominin.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
