      "generated_answer": "The decline of the Roman and Han empires led to increased social instability, during which patriarchal structures often tightened and legal restrictions on women grew. In China, Confucian ideals became more rigidly enforced, and in Rome, women's legal and economic rights contracted compared to the early empire. Thus, the most direct comparative outcome was a decline in the rights of women.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
