      "generated_answer": "The speech highlights France's disregard for African opposition to its Sahara atomic tests, attributing this to Africa's disunity and lack of political weight. Nkrumah argues that this callous disregard proves Great Powers only respect size and influence, which Africa lacks while divided. Therefore, the French viewed Africa as too fragmented to be taken seriously.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
