      "generated_answer": "The Bandung Conference of 1955 gathered newly independent Asian and African nations to promote solidarity and cooperation while resisting pressure to align with either Cold War superpower. Sukarno's emphasis on preserving peace through the collective moral and political strength of Asia and Africa directly reflects the conference's role as a precursor to the Non-Aligned Movement.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
