    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4810",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\n\"We conclude that, in the field of public education, the doctrine of \"separate but equal\" has no place. Separate educational facilities are inherently unequal. Therefore, we hold that the plaintiffs and others similarly situated for whom the actions have been brought are, by reason of the segregation complained of, deprived of the equal protection of the laws guaranteed by the Fourteenth Amendment.\"\nBrown v. Board of Education, 1954\nDesegregation of schools was, in part, a response to unfulfilled promises from which of the following initiatives?\n\nOptions: \nA. The New Deal\nB. The Fair Deal\nC. The New Frontier\nD. Reconstruction\nE. The Square Deal\nF. The Great Society\nG. The Progressive Era\nH. The War on Poverty\nI. The Emancipation Proclamation\nJ. The Civil Rights Act\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **D. Reconstruction**.\n\nThe Brown v. Board of Education decision addressed the unfulfilled promises of the post-Civil War Reconstruction amendments, particularly the Fourteenth Amendment’s guarantee of equal protection under the law. Despite these constitutional promises, the “separate but equal” doctrine had undermined true equality for nearly a century.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
