      "generated_answer": "The gift to Harriet's \"living children\" is contingent on them surviving \"any widow of Stan,\" who could be someone not in being at Walter's death (the classic \"unborn widow\" problem). This violates the common law Rule Against Perpetuities because the interest might vest more than 21 years after all lives in being, rendering the provision void from the start. Therefore, regardless of actual events, Harriet cannot prevail.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
