  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_law_1192",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one of the statements below is false?\n\nOptions: \nA. The war crimes trials at Nuremberg and Tokyo took place immediately after the First World War\nB. The war crimes trials found that \"superior orders\" could not be used as a defence for war crimes or crimes against humanity\nC. The war crimes trials introduced a 'crime against humanity' as an offence\nD. The war crimes trials were held after the Second World War, but before the creation of the United Nations\nE. The war crimes trials were conducted by the United Nations\nF. The war crimes trials at Nuremberg and Tokyo took place in the United States\nG. The war crimes trials did not include the crime of genocide\nH. The war crimes trials held individuals legally responsible for acts such as war crimes and crimes against humanity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
