      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A**.  \n\nUnder the majority rule, continued at-will employment for a substantial period after signing a restrictive covenant constitutes sufficient consideration to make the covenant enforceable. Since the employee remained employed for two years after signing, that period of continued employment satisfies the consideration requirement.  \n\n\\boxed{A}",
