      "generated_answer": "The original package doctrine under the Import-Export Clause and dormant Commerce Clause exempts imported goods from state ad valorem taxation while they remain in the hands of the importer in their original, unbroken packages. The bicycles, still in their shipping crates, are immune from taxation. The tires, having been mingled and stacked with other tires, have lost their immunity and are subject to the tax.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
