      "generated_answer": "The modification is probably unenforceable because it violates the statute of frauds. Under the UCC, a contract for the sale of goods priced at $500 or more must be in writing, and the modified contract (800 gidgets at $4,000/1000 = $4 each, total $3,200) still exceeds that threshold without a new writing. The UCC does not require consideration for modifications, and the parol evidence rule does not bar subsequent oral agreements.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
