      "generated_answer": "The polynomial \\(x^3 + x^2 + c\\) is irreducible over \\(\\mathbb{Z}_3\\) (hence the quotient is a field) if it has no roots in \\(\\mathbb{Z}_3 = \\{0,1,2\\}\\). Evaluating at \\(0,1,2\\) gives \\(f(0)=c\\), \\(f(1)=2+c\\), \\(f(2)=c\\). The only value in \\(\\{0,1,2\\}\\) with no root is \\(c=2\\).\n\n\\boxed{B}",
