      "generated_answer": "The expected value of \\(S\\) is found by setting up a recurrence conditioned on the first random variable. Let \\(f(t)\\) be the expected sum given the first value is \\(t\\). It satisfies \\(f(t) = \\frac{t}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}\\int_0^t f(u)\\,du\\). Differentiating gives \\(f'(t) = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}f(t)\\) with \\(f(0)=0\\), yielding \\(f(t) = e^{t/2} - 1\\). Since \\(X_1\\) is uniform on \\((0,1)\\), the overall expectation is \\(\\int_0^1 (e^{t/2} - 1)\\,dt = 2e^{1/2} - 3 \\approx 0.29744254\\).\n\n\\boxed{I}",
