    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The set of x such that sin(x) < 1/2 in [0,1] is [0, π/6), since sin(π/6) = 1/2 and π/6 ≈ 0.5236 < 1. The condition that cos(x+y) is irrational defines the complement of a countable set of curves, which has Lebesgue measure zero. Thus, the measure of E is simply the area of the rectangle [0, π/6] × [0,1], which is π/6 ≈ 0.5235987667.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
