      "generated_answer": "The characteristic equation is \\(9r^2 + 12r + 4 = 0\\), which factors to \\((3r+2)^2=0\\), giving a repeated root \\(r = -2/3\\). The general solution is \\(y(t) = (c_1 + c_2 t)e^{-2t/3}\\). Applying the initial conditions \\(y(0)=a\\) and \\(y'(0)=-1\\) yields \\(c_1 = a\\) and \\(c_2 = \\frac{2}{3}a - 1\\). The solution becomes \\(y(t) = \\left[a + \\left(\\frac{2}{3}a - 1\\right)t\\right]e^{-2t/3}\\). For \\(y(t)\\) to remain positive for all \\(t \\ge 0\\), the coefficient of \\(t\\) must be non-negative, so \\(\\frac{2}{3}a - 1 \\ge 0 \\Rightarrow a \\ge 1.5\\). The critical value separating solutions that eventually become negative from those always positive is \\(a = 1.5\\).\n\n\\boxed{B}",
