    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The limit is 1.0.\n\nLet \\(S_n = \\sum_{i=1}^n a_i^2\\). Since \\(a_n S_n \\to 1\\) and \\(S_n \\to \\infty\\), we have \\(a_n \\sim 1/S_n\\) and \\(a_n^2 = S_n - S_{n-1} \\sim 1/S_n^2\\), which implies \\(S_n^3 - S_{n-1}^3 \\to 3\\). By Cesàro means, \\(S_n^3/n \\to 3\\), so \\(3n a_n^3 \\sim 3n / S_n^3 \\to 1\\).\n\n\\boxed{E}",
