    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are given \\( z = \\arctan(e^{1 + (1 + x)^2}) \\).  \nFirst, simplify the exponent: \\( 1 + (1 + x)^2 = 1 + 1 + 2x + x^2 = 2 + 2x + x^2 \\).  \nSo \\( z = \\arctan(e^{2 + 2x + x^2}) \\).  \n\nDifferentiate:  \n\\[\n\\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial x} = \\frac{1}{1 + e^{2(2 + 2x + x^2)}} \\cdot e^{2 + 2x + x^2} \\cdot (2 + 2x).\n\\]  \nAt \\( x = 0 \\), exponent is \\( 2 \\), so:  \n\\[\n\\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial x}\\bigg|_{x=0} = \\frac{1}{1 + e^{4}} \\cdot e^{2} \\cdot 2 = \\frac{2e^2}{1 + e^4}.\n\\]  \nNumerically, \\( e^2 \\approx 7.389 \\), \\( e^4 \\approx 54.598 \\), thus:  \n\\[\n\\frac{2(7.389)}{1 + 54.598} \\approx \\frac{14.778}{55.598} \\approx 0.2658.\n\\]  \n\nThis value does not match the given options exactly, so perhaps the original exponent was intended as \\( e^{1 + (1+x)^2} \\) without an extra \\( e \\) in base.  \nIf \\( z = \\arctan\\big(e^{1+(1+x)^2}\\big) \\), then derivative becomes:  \n\\[\n\\frac{2(1+x)e^{1+(1+x)^2}}{1 + e^{2(1+(1+x)^2)}}.\n\\]  \nAt \\( x=0 \\), this is:  \n\\[\n\\frac{2 \\cdot 1 \\cdot e^{1+1}}{1 + e^{2(2)}} = \\frac{2e^2}{1 + e^4} \\approx 0.2658,\n\\]  \nwhich again doesn’t match—possibly there’s a misinterpretation or rounding discrepancy, but among given options, the closest is **0.2896**.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{F}\n\\]",
